Use the first alive fallback proxy when the saved selection is absent.

Source: https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo/pull/3462
Pinned revision: 375dad724b2a5aa6d6a24d54797fb02b28d2c520

Keep the PR's production change and both regression tests. Add a source-reference
comment and deterministic checks for provider removal/return, manual selection
priority, an empty provider, all-dead members and normal first-alive selection.
The saved preference survives a provider refresh; the first entry still needs
an actual health check rather than a vote of confidence.

diff --git a/adapter/outboundgroup/fallback.go b/adapter/outboundgroup/fallback.go
--- a/adapter/outboundgroup/fallback.go
+++ b/adapter/outboundgroup/fallback.go
@@ -120,6 +120,20 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	// Based on https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo/pull/3462.
+	// A missing selection does not make the first proxy magically alive.
+	// The selected proxy is not in the group: it was renamed or removed, it was
+	// restored from the cache file under a name the group no longer has, or its
+	// provider has not loaded yet. Pick as if nothing were selected, and keep
+	// the selection so it applies again once a provider lists the proxy.
+	if len(f.selected) != 0 {
+		for _, proxy := range proxies {
+			if proxy.AliveForTestUrl(f.testUrl) {
+				return proxy
+			}
+		}
+	}
+
 	return proxies[0]
 }
 
